  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall be maintained in accordance with the following approved plans and documents:\r\rLocation Plan - PP-14644491v1\rBlock Plan - 400\rExisting Site Plan - 100100\rProposed Site Plan - 200100\rExisting (Retrospective) Ground Floor Plan - 200201\rExisting (Retrospective) Ground Floor Context Plan - 200202\rExisting (Retrospective) First Floor Plan - 200203\rExisting (Retrospective) Roof Plan - 200204\rExisting (Retrospective) Elevations Plan - 200301\rExisting (Retrospective) Section Plan - 200401\rFire Statement\rFlood Risk Assessment\rFlood Map\rNoise and Disturbance Plan\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "The use of the property as a House in Multiple Occupation hereby approved shall be occupied by a maximum of 5 people at any one time and shall not be subdivided or occupied as self-contained units.\r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "No independent cooking or laundry facilities shall be installed in any of the respective bedrooms and the communal kitchen / dining room shall be retained in perpetuity.\r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "Within 2 months of this permission, details of HMO communal refuse storage facilities, including facilities for the recycling of waste to satisfy the future number of occupiers on site, shall be provided within the development in accordance with the London Borough of Enfield - Household Recycling and Waste Planning Guidance for New Developments (February 2024). In particular, waste collection vehicles must be able to get within 25m of the refuse storage point. Residents should not have to carry waste further than 30m.\r\r\rReason: In order to facilitate efficient, safe and clean removal of household refuse, to ensure the appropriate location and accessibility of refuse storage, and to maintain safety on the highway.",
    "Within two months of this permission, details of the required 5 cycle parking spaces shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority.\r\rThese details should demonstrate:\r\rLocation: Near entrances or main access,\rDesign: Stands\rSecurity: Secure, overlooked, well-lit,\rFull enclosed: 4 walls and a roof,\rAccessibility: 1.2m wide, Step-free, no obstructions.\r\rThe cycle parking spaces shall be fully constructed in accordance with the details stated above prior to first occupation and shall thereafter be retained for the lifetime of the development.\r\rReason: To ensure that adequate cycle parking facilities are provided to conform to Enfield DMD policy 45 and promote sustainable modes of transport.\r"
  ],
